From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unom <packages@unom.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:57:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] punktfunk: stamp pfhdr40

A host offers a tiled modifier on a planar capture only to a gamescope that
lists them: an older one lists LINEAR alone, which fixates the consumer's
default.
---
 src/meson.build | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 395c5482..af0cb943 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -232,7 +232,8 @@ vcs_tag = run_command(vcs_tag_cmd, check: false).stdout().strip()
 #   +pfhdr37 — …and a refresh with a fraction (-r 59.94) runs to the millihertz
 #   +pfhdr38 — …and Intel is told a LINEAR capture image is exported (Xe2 compressed it)
 #   +pfhdr39 — …and a planar capture's chroma starts on a 16-row boundary on Intel
-version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr39' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
+#   +pfhdr40 — …and a planar capture dmabuf takes a tiled modifier its consumer accepts, on Intel
+version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr40' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
 
 gamescope_version_conf = configuration_data()
 gamescope_version_conf.set('VCS_TAG', version_tag)
-- 
2.56.0

